-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
<YOUR_HSM_RSA_PUBLIC_KEY>

This public key must be exported directly from the HSM using the key reference.
Do NOT use a separately generated key — it must match the private key stored in the HSM.

To obtain this file:
  1. List HSM keys to find the correct key reference:
     CLOUDHSM_PIN=<cu_user>:<password> CLOUDHSM_ROLE=crypto-user \
       /opt/cloudhsm/bin/cloudhsm-cli key list --filter attr.label=rsa001

  2. Export public key using the key reference (not the label):
     CLOUDHSM_PIN=<cu_user>:<password> CLOUDHSM_ROLE=crypto-user \
       /opt/cloudhsm/bin/cloudhsm-cli key generate-file \
       --filter key-reference=<0xKEY_REFERENCE> \
       --encoding pem \
       --path rsa001.pub

  3. Verify the fingerprint matches what is registered in the Virtru admin console:
     openssl rsa -pubin -in rsa001.pub -outform DER | \
       openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | basenc --base64url | tr -d '='

IMPORTANT: Use ONLY one key reference at a time. If multiple keys share
the same label, the CLI will error. Always specify by key reference.
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----